<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10678"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 06, 2005 - 9:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->G B S O A P 7-T N L T R D E I T B S F A V 1 4 <BR> <BR>I love words. <BR> <BR>Puzzles? They’re O.K. -- when I’ve got time to kill and I know the rules. <BR> <BR>When only the killer knows the rules, time runs out. <BR> <BR>G B S O A P 7-T N L T R D E I T B S F A V 1 4 <BR> <BR>This string of 20 letters, 3 numerals and a dash was received by the Wichita Eagle on March 2004, according to the link provided by Bojo: <BR> <BR><a href="http://aolsvc.news.aol.com/news/article.adp?id=20050225192709990002#puzzle" target=_top>http://aolsvc.news.aol.com/news/article.adp?id=200 50225192709990002#puzzle</a> <BR> <BR>While the photo does not indicate the scale, the characters appear to be similar to the hand stenciling used on the Post Toasties® box. <BR> <BR>Is it a cryptogram? Is it ascii? Is it an anagram? <BR>If there’s math involved, bring your abacus and count me out! <BR> <BR>G B S O A P 7-T N L T R D E I T B S F A V 1 4 <BR> <BR>1-7 4 B G I N S/ B S A/ A F V E T/ D L R <BR> <BR>OK,  I’ve come up with the month and year of the Otero murders, <BR>Boy Scouts where he learned to tie the clove hitch, <BR>the Air Force &#40; you just know he’ll claim THEY trained him to kill&#41;, <BR>his real initials and… what the Hell is TTP?... PTT?... TPT?... OH WAIT! <BR>He’s already in jail. <BR> <BR>Unless this puzzle is about an unsolved case, why bother?   <BR> <BR>G B S O A P 7-T N L T R D E I T B S F A V 1 4 <BR> <BR>G     S O A P 7-T N L T R D E I T     S F A V 1 4       BB <BR> <BR>G        O A    7-T N L T R D E           S F A V 1 4       SPIT <BR> <BR>G            A    7-T     L T R D E           S F A V 1 4       ON <BR> <BR>                      7-T     L T     D                     A V 1 4       FAGERS <BR> <BR>                      7-T     L T     D                     A V 1 4 <BR> <BR>Now I’d like to buy a vowel. <BR> <BR>Actually I’d prefer a K. <BR> <BR>That way I could get… <BR> <BR>BT”K” SPIT ON FAGERS <BR> <BR>…with <BR> <BR>B 7 – L T D S A V 1 4 <BR> <BR>… as my leftovers. <BR> <BR>SPIT? <BR> <BR>When I first heard about this: <BR> <BR>B     Post <BR>T o a s t i e s®	 <BR>K <BR> <BR>I came up with this:		 <BR> <BR>BTK sPiTs at ote®os  <BR> <BR>Of course, another way to look at th… Whoops, I just ran out of patience. <BR> <BR>Congratulations! If you are still reading this you have less Adult Attention Deficit Disorder than me. <BR> <BR>I’m going to pop a Ritalin® and try to organize my garage now.      <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
