<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11845"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 4:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ember, <BR>If------GBSOAP7-TNLTRDEITBSFA14 ------  <BR>is decoded as being OFFSET:  0 <BR>then I take it to mean each letter and digit stands for itself, and they are unscrambled by choosing some letters from the left and then from the right. <BR>1-74 PA NTSB GVT LIED TO AF BRS. <BR>To me, it reads: <BR>January 1974 - PA  NTSB  <BR>Government lied to Air Force brass. <BR>Could that be true? <BR>Date: January 1974 <BR>Piper Model: PA <BR>NTSB:  National Transportation Safety Bureau  &#40;for ID&#41; <BR>GVT:  Government <BR>LIED TO:  lied to <BR>AF BRS:   Air Force Brass <BR>MAIL CALL FROM CANADA<!--/Text--></td></tr>
