</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 11:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have a different, tho&#39; equally convoluted solution to : &#34;GBSOAP7-TNLTRDEITBSFA14&#34;. <BR> <BR>I used various calculations, similar to yours, only adding 3 where the covalent was sub-zero. Then substituting a simple Gareth-Penn logrithym to the whole number ratio, I get; <BR> <BR>&#34;I dropped my pants- in front of Army headaquarters, just for the hell of it!&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
